      "text": "Epilepsy clinic letter\nConsultation: 05 March 2025\nPatient: Laura Chen, aged 28\n\nDear colleague,\n\nLaura attended our clinic following referral for episodic paroxysmal sensory symptoms.\n\nShe describes episodes of sudden visual scintillations followed by dizziness and paresthesia in the left hand lasting 10 to 15 minutes, occurring roughly weekly, with the latest episode on 28 February 2025. Her clinical assessment is challenging. The differential diagnosis includes focal sensory epilepsy, migraine aura without headache, or vestibular events. I cannot establish a definitive diagnosis of epilepsy today, and the clinical picture remains indeterminate. She takes no anti-seizure medications.\n\nWe arranged brain MRI and routine outpatient EEG. Follow-up in four months.\n\nLaura says she has never lost awareness during her sensory episodes. Her mother reports that Laura did not respond to her voice during the episode on 28 February and believes awareness was lost. Laura disputes this account. I have not resolved this reporter disagreement; neither report settles the epilepsy versus migraine differential.\n"
    }
  ],
